course: dictionary
lesson: 1986
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compress means to press or squeeze something so it takes up less space. A sponge can be compressed, and so can the air in a bike tyre. The words around a word are its context, and they give clues. Look for clues like «air», «tyre» or «squeeze» to find the meaning.
explain: «She was fine after a cold compress, but Tom was sent to the head and his mates went very quiet.» Here, compress is a thing you can put on a bump, not an action. A compress is a pad of cloth, often cold or warm and wet, pressed on the body to ease pain or swelling. The word «cold» and the idea of a bump are your clues.
explain: Compress can also mean to make something shorter. In computing, to compress a file makes it smaller so it is quicker to send or store. «Compress the story into one page» means make the story shorter. Ask yourself: does the sentence want something squeezed, shrunk, or shortened? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Compress means to press or squeeze something so it takes up less space.
fact: A compress is a pad of cloth, often cold or warm and wet, pressed on the body to ease pain or swelling.
fact: «Compressed air» is air squeezed into a smaller space, as in a bike tyre or a spray can.
fact: In computing, to compress a file makes it smaller so it is quicker to send or store.
fact: A good check is to swap in squeeze or shrink and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «She was fine after a cold compress, but Tom was sent to the head.» What is a compress here? | *A pad of cloth, cold or wet, pressed on the body to ease pain | Small tent for camping | A loud noise | A kind of sweet
exercise: Ben needs to email a big folder quickly. What does it mean to compress the folder? | *Make it smaller so it is quicker to send | Make it bigger and heavier | Paint it a new colour
exercise: «The air in the bike tyre is compressed.» What does compressed mean here? | Made louder | Spread out to fill more space | *Squeezed into less space | Turned into water
test: «Compress the story into one page.» What does compress mean here? | Draw a picture of it | *Make it shorter | Make it longer | Read it out loud slowly
test: In «a cold compress», what kind of word is compress? | An adjective | A verb | *A noun | An adverb
exam: Ruby says compress means to make something bigger. What is the correct meaning? | To make it bigger | To freeze it | To paint it | *To press or squeeze it so it takes up less space
